{
	"id": "errors-are-invisible",
	"text": "This problem is fractal, of course. Our call to getCart, which presumably returns a Promise<Cart>, is just as opaque. To know how it might fail, we have to read its implementation. And then, we must recursively read any definitions it references, and so on. Perhaps we'd rather trust the docstring, if there is one, and pray it's up to date.",
	"code": "async function checkout(cartId: string): Promise<Order> {\n  const cart = await getCart(cartId)\n  const payment = await charge(cart)\n  const shipment = await ship(payment)\n  return shipment\n}",
